    {
      "slug": "silk-road-dinner",
      "title": "Silk Road Dinner",
      "section": "dinners",
      "date": "March 2026",
      "blurb": "We followed the old trade routes from east to west, course by course, along with the stories that travelled the same roads as the spices. I dug into the archaeobotanical record to work out where and when certain plants were domesticated, which direction they travelled and when they arrived. My friend Airas Sanchez Keller took that research and designed a map of the Silk Road showing the place and time each plant was domesticated, and we built the menu using only ingredients that would have been available along the route at the time. It was a fantastically interesting project to research, and it made for a genuinely enriching evening for our guests. Special thanks to the [Storytellers Club Zurich](https://zurichstorytellers.ch) for taking part and bringing the stories of the Silk Road to life.",
