      "slug": "earth-beneath-us-dinner",
      "title": "Earth Beneath Us Dinner",
      "section": "dinners",
      "date": "September 2025",
      "blurb": "An evening about what sits under our feet. We looked at the earth two ways: as the living medium that grows our food, and as a source of flavour in its own right \u2014 right down to the dishes the food is served on. We cooked vegetables buried in clay and others in hot springs, and gave a good part of the night to the earth's great companion, fungi \u2014 mushrooms throughout, and koji. Dessert came on tableware we made ourselves, from clay dug nearby.",
